# NOT a dinit service - nvidia-hibernate/resume/suspend.service on the
# live CachyOS box are systemd-logind sleep hooks (Before=/After=
# systemd-suspend.service etc), not boot-time daemons. Real commands,
# verified via `systemctl cat`:
#
#   nvidia-sleep.sh suspend    (before sleep)
#   nvidia-sleep.sh hibernate  (before hibernate)
#   nvidia-sleep.sh resume     (after either)
#
# This dinit.d setup uses seatd (see subsys/seatd), not
# elogind/systemd-logind, so there is no equivalent hook directory
# (elogind would have honored /usr/lib/elogind/system-sleep/ the same
# way systemd does /usr/lib/systemd/system-sleep/ - seatd doesn't do
# sleep orchestration at all, it's just the seat/device-access backend).
#
# Whatever actually triggers suspend on the Void box (a Hyprland
# keybind, a power-button script, swayidle-equivalent) needs to call
# these three lines directly, in order, around its own suspend call:
#
#   /usr/bin/nvidia-sleep.sh suspend
#   <the real suspend trigger, e.g. doas zzz, or writing to
#    /sys/power/state - find/decide this when the Void box exists>
#   /usr/bin/nvidia-sleep.sh resume
#
# Nothing to add to subsys/ for this one until that trigger script
# exists - then these three lines go inside it, not here.
